# CORTE CERO
# 2:00 exactly / 160 BPM / 80 bars / seed 3181 / play once.
# Every source excites a feedback return. No dry oscillator reaches the master.
# 00:00 ARC: establish the pressure grid.
# 00:30 FRACTURE: narrow the bands and shear the grid.
# 01:00 WHITE ROOM: open the noise and cut the reverberated mass.
# 01:30 BLACKOUT: recover the pulse, overload it, extinguish the output.
# q is reciprocal Q: smaller values make a narrower, more resonant band.
# Revision 3: independent post-return choppers, no shared master gate.
# Revision 2: four independent returns per block; continuously moving controls.
# Sub fundamentals descend to 26 Hz. All excitation remains inside feedback.
# Outer h/r order is intentional. Output v stays outside the return gain g.
# LOOP is disabled by the Pieces preset. Cmd+. or Escape disconnects everything.
!vc

# One beat = 0.375 seconds. The last tick ends exactly at the beat boundary.
beata=(
 s145^43'0.15v0>2.8>0'0.15e0p-0.15>0.15'0.15
 0.1875n1v0.32p0.7e0031'0.035
 0.335n1v0.22p-0.7e0031'0.04
)
beatb=(
 q160^39'0.14v0>2.9>0'0.14e0p0.25>-0.25'0.14
 0.09375n1v0.5p-0.8e0031'0.025
 0.335n2v0.45p0.8e0031'0.04
)
beatc=(
 n1v1.8p0e0061'0.14
 0.1875q?[330:3300]v0.75p-0.8e0031'0.035
 0.335n1v0.9p0.8e0031'0.04
)
beatd=(
 s135^41'0.14v0>3.1>0'0.14e0p-0.2>0.2'0.14
 0.1875s95^39'0.09v2.2p-0.2e0061
 0.335n1v0.8p0.6e0031'0.04
)


